# Nothing in here is servable.
#
# lib/path.php answered HTTP 200 over the web on a real install. It contains no secret —
# it is in the public repository — but a file the bridge includes is a file an attacker
# can read to learn exactly how paths are validated before trying to get past it, and the
# directory is a natural place for the next person to drop something that does matter.
#
# The deny list in the parent .htaccess cannot cover this: index.php has to stay servable,
# so ".php" cannot be denied there.
Require all denied
